PRE-TABLE AMENDMENT, PASS 9 -- its own file (mtime against part9/driver.log is the order witness).

SECTION 17 -- a conjunction over two held lvalues, and what pass 9 corrected in the record.
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Opus seat (predicted before its build, then measured on its clone): `&& !(pending_timer1 &&
  pending_timer2)' at the TxICR guard passes every row -- each count is held non-zero in its OWN
  session (pend1/pendn1 arm timer 1, pend2/pendn2 timer 2) and no session arms both.  Both counts
  are body-read (in closure) and the joint state is guest-reachable.  The value-domain statement
  held each lvalue's VALUES; it did not hold the reachable TUPLES.  Rows `pendboth arm' (T2ICR
  0x31), `pendboth arm1' (T1ICR 0x31: both non-zero at the wide write), `pendboth decl', `pendboth
  rb'.  Shape verified by hand on the restored part-8 clone (0x31 / 0x31 / declined / 0x31).
* Record corrections applied in place (grok, codex, fable5): the contract's TxCTL paragraph said
  bits 2-3 were E, no row on the memcpy path, the path operator-only -- beside the shipped `rb
  t*ctl b27' rows and the guest st.d premise; TxICR bit 3 restored to the dead-bit list; the
  pass-8 header's 171 -> 186 (190); eight answering seats; seven cells; eight measurements; the
  quit is still sent after a missed token.
* Instrument hygiene (codex, grok): rd() re-checks the token after its loop (it could land in the
  final read and the wait return 'timeout' falsely); cval() takes `alive' so a decl row graded
  after the guest died says so.  No row changed by either.
* Disclosed by NAME now (the stop condition's remainder): TxCTL bits 0-1 = 2, the overflow count
  at 2-7 and 9-15, TxCTL 0xff, TxICR 0x37 and bit 3, pending between 2 and 9999 and above, idata
  = 2 or any constant no row drives.
* Opus interim 2A-2C, folded before the table: `ovfhi* arm/rb' pinned the EXACT byte 0x81 while the
  count advances one per DELIVERED callback -- a descheduled emulator exits the poll at 9 (0x91)
  and the row reds for an unnamed reason.  Masked to bits 7 and 0 (count >= 8 AND CEN); the
  mutant's 0x80 still reds, RE-MEASURED below as a control rather than derived from part 8.
  The `if False:' waitpid relic is deleted; os.write, the one unbounded call, has its sentence;
  the pass-8 CHANGELOG sentence claiming cval() covered the death half is corrected.
